    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0350" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg230"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-11-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my dispatch No. 112 of
                    October 4, I inclose herewith copy of a note which I addressed to the minister
                    of foreign affairs on the 30th of October, again calling his attention to the
                    dilatoriness of the Liang Kuang viceroy in regard to the stopping of the
                    anti-American agitation in the Province of Kuang-tung.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d239-a1.xml" xpointer="d239-a1"/>
